Identify all unique adult patients (age ≥18 years) with CKD G3a–G5 and qualifying CKD evidence documented during the last 60 months from the query execution date.

Include ONLY patients who are NOT on dialysis and have NO documented ESKD/ESRD diagnosis or evidence of dialysis treatment.

Search ALL care settings. Do not require hospitalization, an AKI diagnosis, or any other associated diagnosis.

CKD IDENTIFICATION — USE LABORATORY CRITERIA OR ICD-10-CM CODES:

A. Laboratory-based identification:
- At least two outpatient or otherwise clinically stable eGFR measurements <60 mL/min/1.73 m², separated by ≥3 months.
- At least one qualifying measurement must fall within the last 60 months. Earlier results may support chronicity.
- Do not use eGFR measured during AKI to establish CKD or assign CKD stage.
- Classify CKD using stable eGFR:
  G3a: 45 to <60 mL/min/1.73 m².
  G3b: 30 to <45 mL/min/1.73 m².
  G4: 15 to <30 mL/min/1.73 m².
  G5: <15 mL/min/1.73 m².
- Record the supporting eGFR values and dates.

OR

B. ICD-10-CM-based identification:
Include patients with any of the following codes documented in encounter diagnoses or an active problem list during the last 60 months:

N18.30 — CKD stage 3, unspecified
OR N18.31 — CKD stage 3a
OR N18.32 — CKD stage 3b
OR N18.4 — CKD stage 4
OR N18.5 — CKD stage 5

- A qualifying ICD-10-CM code alone is sufficient for cohort identification.
- Do not require laboratory confirmation for code-identified patients.
- Label patients without supporting longitudinal laboratory evidence as “code-identified; laboratory confirmation unavailable.”
- Do not infer G3a versus G3b from N18.30 alone.
- Preserve code-derived and laboratory-derived stages separately and flag discrepancies.

MANDATORY EXCLUSIONS — NO ESKD AND NO DIALYSIS:

Apply these exclusions regardless of whether CKD was identified through laboratory results or diagnosis codes.

Exclude any patient with ANY of the following documented during the last 60 months or in available earlier history:

- ICD-10-CM N18.6: end-stage renal disease.
- ICD-10-CM Z99.2: dependence on renal dialysis.
- An affirmative ESKD/ESRD diagnosis in encounter diagnoses, problem lists, nephrology notes, discharge summaries, or other clinical documentation.
- A completed dialysis procedure record or dialysis procedure note.
- Clinical documentation confirming receipt of hemodialysis, peritoneal dialysis, continuous renal replacement therapy, or another dialysis treatment.

Search diagnosis codes, procedure codes, procedure records, dialysis flowsheets, and clinical/procedure notes. Do not rely on diagnosis codes alone to identify dialysis.

For this strict no-documented-dialysis cohort, prior temporary dialysis for AKI also counts as an exclusion.

Do not interpret dialysis education, future dialysis planning, access placement alone, an unperformed or canceled dialysis order, or a negated statement such as “not on dialysis” as evidence that dialysis occurred.

Do not exclude CKD G5 solely because eGFR is <15 or N18.5 is present; require a separate ESKD or dialysis exclusion flag.

Flag incomplete records or uncertain ESKD/dialysis status for separate review rather than assuming absence.

FINAL BOOLEAN LOGIC:

Age ≥18 years
AND qualifying CKD evidence within the last 60 months
AND (
    laboratory-based CKD criteria
    OR ICD-10-CM = N18.30
    OR ICD-10-CM = N18.31
    OR ICD-10-CM = N18.32
    OR ICD-10-CM = N18.4
    OR ICD-10-CM = N18.5
)
AND NOT (
    ICD-10-CM = N18.6
    OR ICD-10-CM = Z99.2
    OR documented ESKD/ESRD diagnosis
    OR completed dialysis procedure
    OR procedure note confirming dialysis
    OR clinical documentation confirming dialysis treatment
)

OUTPUT:

Return one row per unique eligible patient with:
- Patient identifier.
- Age at first qualifying date.
- First qualifying CKD date within the last 60 months.
- Laboratory-derived CKD stage and corresponding measurement date.
- Code-derived CKD stage.
- Identification method: laboratory only, ICD code only, or both.
- Qualifying ICD-10-CM codes and dates.
- Supporting eGFR values and dates.
- ESKD/dialysis screening result: “No documented ESKD or dialysis in available records.”
- Missing-data or stage-discrepancy flags.

Return patients with uncertain exclusion status separately for review.

Do not apply any care-setting restriction or duplicate patients across encounters.
